WHAT THIS LICENSE COVERS
------------------------
  code/          this release's API and the model definition code
  models/        the backbone checkpoint, TM head, EC head and align head weights
  reproduce/     the reproduction scripts and their recorded results
  README.md, models/MODEL_CARD.md and the other documentation in this tree

WHAT IT DOES NOT COVER (third-party material, under its own terms)
------------------------------------------------------------------
  reproduce/ec_deer_figure7/data/
      DEER's Figure 7 benchmark data (Liu et al., Cell Host & Microbe 2026).
      Licensed by its authors under the Apache License 2.0 -- a permissive
      license that we cannot and do not restrict. Those files remain under
      Apache-2.0 for everyone, including commercial users. See that directory's
      LICENSE.DEER and README.md.

  pfam_data/Pfam-A.clans.tsv
      Pfam data (Pfam release 36.0), released by the Pfam consortium under
      CC0 1.0 (public domain). Redistributed here unchanged; it is NOT covered
      by the noncommercial terms above and remains CC0 for everyone, including
      commercial users. Cite: Mistry, J. et al. Nucleic Acids Res. 49,
      D412-D419 (2021).

  PfamScan and the Pfam-A HMM library
      Not bundled, on purpose. PfamScan (pfam_scan.pl) is GPL-2.0-or-later, so
      bundling it would pull GPL code into this package; the HMM library is
      300 MB. code/scripts/setup_pfam.sh downloads both on demand into
      pfam_data/, where they stay under their own licenses.

  The ProtT5-XL encoder (Rostlab/prot_t5_xl_uniref50), which the backbone is
      built on, is fetched at run time and is not redistributed here. The
      ProtTrans project is MIT-licensed.

